<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for March 21.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for March 21.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, on Thursday announced the following forecasts and data for gas use in the period March 19 to 21.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Mar 19 (actual) 252 mcm, 59 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 20 (forecast) 255 mcm, 60 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 21 (forecast) 255 mcm, 60 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Mar 19 (actual) 7.7 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.7 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 20 (forecast) 7.3 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.8 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 21 (forecast) 6.1 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.9 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption on Thursday, with none expected on Friday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
